{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted","id":1390318,"title":"I need advice on how to run a BATTLE in exalted.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-20T10:20:30-07:00","id":1390318,"title":"I need advice on how to run a BATTLE in exalted.","content":"Hello all.<br /> The advice I need is in how to do this mechanically. Do I run the armies as two separate BATTLE groups? How do I handle different troop types in the same army? Is each type it's own group?<br /> Another question is how does a low-tech setting handle magical super beings who can emulate 21st century black-ops teams and artillery barrages? How will this affect stories with war and lord of the rings style BATTLEs as a focus?<br /> <br /> I eagerly await your advice on these matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","name":"Hyper Prime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1131_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T10:30:50-07:00","id":1390322,"title":"","content":"Well firstly, what kind of battle is it? Is it a super huge thing with 20,000 soldiers spread across an entire city and multiple fortresses, or like a relatively small group with archer support attacking a town?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T10:46:10-07:00","id":1390323,"title":"","content":"For groups composed of different types of troops, weigh whether you feel the differences are enough to be mechanically or dramatically relevant. Infantry and archers might be able to just be one BG. Infantry and cavalry, probably they should be their own BGs, given the significance of mounted status.<br /> <br /> How does the setting handle juiced-up supers? Well, some can still be BGs with Might, a BG stat reflecting magical army strength. Exalts are more or less never going to be BGs, though, unless somehow you're fielding a hundred Dragonblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T10:59:25-07:00","id":1390331,"title":"","content":"I'd run it like the first combat <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372266#post1372266\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> A bit like a Dynasty Warriors game.<br /> <br /> If the PCs are winning in their personal fights, then the army in the background is also winning. If the PCs get pushed back, the army gets pushed back too.<br /> <br /> If the enemy makes a good War roll they might pull off a reversal of fortunes, causing the PC's army to be driven back even as the PCs themselves cleave their way unstoppably forwards.<br /> <br /> I would group all allied troops into a single battlegroup. Yes, you have archers and cavalry and heavy infantry and skirmishers... Exalted doesn't meaningfully discriminate. If it's battlegroup on battlegroup then keep it simple -- narrate it evocatively, but keep the dice rolling and book keeping simple. I'd even group troops vast distances apart into one battlegroup so long as it's two armies squaring off in a straight clash (if it's four different armies and a mile high behemoth squaring off over the sprawling ruins of a first age metropolis as mutated beast-folk despertaly try to escape and elite fae dance through the chaos, then multiple battle groups is probably the way to go). Magnitude damage can represent entire sections of the army being driven back (you free the Market District by routing the Heavy Infantry, but the Skirmishers still control the docks).<br /> <br /> PCs and their kewl powaz are going to dominate. Whether it's with black-ops air strikes or being <i>really</i> good with a sword, the battle turns on their prowess. For an idea of the feel of this, check out the Illiad (or the 2004 Brad Pitt film &quot;Troy&quot;), or the Dynasty Warriors computer games (frankly, <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=7DwmSr4df4o\" target=\"_blank\">Hyrule Warriors is far and away the best</a>).<br /> <br /> Don't expect a hundred farmers with bronze swords to stop the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T11:24:33-07:00","id":1390344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390331#post1390331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd run it like the first combat <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372266#post1372266\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> PCs and their kewl powaz are going to dominate. Whether it's with black-ops air strikes or being <i>really</i> good with a sword, the battle turns on their prowess. For an idea of the feel of this, check out the Illiad (or the 2004 Brad Pitt film &quot;Troy&quot;), or the Dynasty Warriors computer games (frankly, <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=7DwmSr4df4o\" target=\"_blank\">Hyrule Warriors is far and away the best</a>).</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm afraid of is that the whole spectable(??) of 1400 century warfare being corrupted by asymentrical pre-emptive modern artillery barrages or warhammer 40K style spacemarine kill-teams.<br /> Dynasty warriors or Troy-esque heroes getting stuck in is fine, thats what I would prefere. It's the other things I don't like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","name":"Hyper Prime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1131_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T11:27:56-07:00","id":1390345,"title":"","content":"Who/what are the PCs? Because PCs can have very different effects on the battles depending. If you've got a Solar sorcerer throwing around Death Ray, you'll want to approach it very differently to if you've got a Dawn with a bunch of war charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T11:39:27-07:00","id":1390351,"title":"","content":"It really depends on what you want from the scene.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, more battle groups offers greater verisimilitude. It makes battles less of a duel between two generals and involves a whole bunch of named lieutenants and sub-commanders to lead specialist formations and since you'll probably outpace the number of war orientated Exalts available to either side you're probably going to need mortal officers with named character status who have a very decent chance of dying if they find themselves unable to get away from an enemy battle group after a lucky roll.<br /> <br /> A more gruelling battle, such as a siege might take place over the course of several scenes interspersed with non-combat scenes that may be critical to later strategic success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T13:04:20-07:00","id":1390363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyper Prime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390344#post1390344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'm afraid of is that the whole spectable(??) of 1400 century warfare being corrupted by asymentrical pre-emptive modern artillery barrages or warhammer 40K style spacemarine kill-teams.<br /> Dynasty warriors or Troy-esque heroes getting stuck in is fine, thats what I would prefere. It's the other things I don't like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Spectacle.<br /> <br /> And if your PCs are Solars with Tiger Warriors, high quality Twilight-crafted gear, and maybe some First Age essence weaponry... it could very well be as asymmetrical as WH40k vs IRL Romans Legionnaires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T13:42:18-07:00","id":1390368,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Hyper Prime;n1390318]Hello all.<br /> The advice I need is in how to do this mechanically. Do I run the armies as two separate BATTLE groups? How do I handle different troop types in the same army? Is each type it's own group?<br /> <br /> For running a big battle it depends how you want it to feel, and what opponents there are. If it's just one general and their massive army, I suggest not running it as just one guy and a huge battlegroup. Depending on what PCs you have it will be over very quickly with likewise very little in the way of tactical and strategic depth. Then again if it's just two big forces fighting in a featureless open field that they form big battle lines on and then charge at eachother, that might be the way to do it.<br /> <br /> If there is terrain around, or buildings, then I can offer more advise, but at this point there's literally hundreds of things I could suggest that would be 100% useless to you because they don't apply to your specific situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyper Prime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted#post1390318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question is how does a low-tech setting handle magical super beings who can emulate 21st century black-ops teams and artillery barrages? How will this affect stories with war and lord of the rings style BATTLEs as a focus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally by having those things themselves. Creation is not really a low-fantasy world. Although there are definitely places in the world with less magic, or who don't/can't apply it in a martial way, there's lots of places that can. The nation of Lookshy has a fleet of first age airships and elite marines called the Skyguard, they also have soldiers in fantastical power armor, first age fortresses, and flying single-person aircraft called Windblades.<br /> <br /> There are also a lot less modern/sci-fi feeling things that make conflict in Creation different. For example a lot of spirits can become immaterial, so while you might want a spec-ops style squad to sneak in someplace, it might be way better to have an invisible immaterial spirit go spying for you. On the other hand the people of Creation know about these things, and have their own magics set up to deal with them for the most part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T14:30:39-07:00","id":1390383,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for the very insightful input. You have given me a lot to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","name":"Hyper Prime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1131_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T16:04:53-07:00","id":1390401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390331#post1390331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd run it like the first combat <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372266#post1372266\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> A bit like a Dynasty Warriors game.<br /> <br /> If the PCs are winning in their personal fights, then the army in the background is also winning. If the PCs get pushed back, the army gets pushed back too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite how DW shakes out all the time. It has a track record for making you babysit allied officers or else, and in earlier games, it was particularly worrisome for being on the opposite side of the map without the capacity to whistle up a horse from nowhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the enemy makes a good War roll they might pull off a reversal of fortunes, causing the PC's army to be driven back even as the PCs themselves cleave their way unstoppably forwards. </div> </div> </div>That seems like it might skip over a bit too much action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would group all allied troops into a single battlegroup. Yes, you have archers and cavalry and heavy infantry and skirmishers... Exalted doesn't meaningfully discriminate. </div> </div> </div>Aren't you supposed to discriminate when you have disparate statistics and capabilities? That's the one occasion when splitting up the force into groups makes perfect sense, because the aggregated masses don't function the same way. Too much aggregation gives you BattleTech Infantry Abstraction issues, where having long-range weapons makes the short-range weapons reach further and expects you to average ammunition types even in one-shot weapons that should only have anti-vehicular ammunition (oh hello LAW).<br /> <br /> ...Ahem. Sorry, that's a long-standing sore point for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's battlegroup on battlegroup then keep it simple -- narrate it evocatively, but keep the dice rolling and book keeping simple. I'd even group troops vast distances apart into one battlegroup so long as it's two armies squaring off in a straight clash (if it's four different armies and a mile high behemoth squaring off over the sprawling ruins of a first age metropolis as mutated beast-folk despertaly try to escape and elite fae dance through the chaos, then multiple battle groups is probably the way to go). Magnitude damage can represent entire sections of the army being driven back (you free the Market District by routing the Heavy Infantry, but the Skirmishers still control the docks).<br /> <br /> PCs and their kewl powaz are going to dominate. Whether it's with black-ops air strikes or being <i>really</i> good with a sword, the battle turns on their prowess. For an idea of the feel of this, check out the Illiad (or the 2004 Brad Pitt film &quot;Troy&quot;), or the Dynasty Warriors computer games (frankly, <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=7DwmSr4df4o\" target=\"_blank\">Hyrule Warriors is far and away the best</a>).<br /> <br /> Don't expect a hundred farmers with bronze swords to stop the PCs. </div> </div> </div>Or even a hundred elite troops with the best equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T16:55:54-07:00","id":1390413,"title":"","content":"When it comes to if troops should be divided or not, I consider narrative role more important than the stats. For example, if a sorcerer has two weeks before a battle and summons 10 different kinds of first circle demon I'm not going to run 10 individual characters because they're cannon fodder. <br /> <br /> With mortals, your heavy cavalry and your skirmishers are probably from very different walks of life which could affect how replaceable their casualties are and who you're upsetting if they get wiped out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T17:22:37-07:00","id":1390420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390331#post1390331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't expect a hundred farmers with bronze swords to stop the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a mechanical assessment, or a statement of priorities to dissuade actually making the attempt?<br /> <br /> [Note: the &quot;farmer&quot; with a bronze sword is necessarily a wealthy landowner, and quite likely to devote much of their life towards developing personal sword skills and drilling with neighbours so that an effective contribution to the defence of the homeland can be made. The status of being a farmer with a bronze sword is likely contingent on that obligation.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-20-2020, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T19:38:39-07:00","id":1390441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390420#post1390420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this a mechanical assessment, or a statement of priorities to dissuade actually making the attempt?<br /> <br /> [Note: the &quot;farmer&quot; with a bronze sword is necessarily a wealthy landowner, and quite likely to devote much of their life towards developing personal sword skills and drilling with neighbours so that an effective contribution to the defence of the homeland can be made. The status of being a farmer with a bronze sword is likely contingent on that obligation.]</div> </div> </div> </div>In past editions, soldiers that split duties between drill and farming were passingly mentioned as being the solid rank and file that still fell as regular extras, so that might inform a mechanical expectation in this case. I know it informed my response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T01:02:44-07:00","id":1390509,"title":"","content":"Well a guy who turns up to a battle with no equipment except a sword is clearly a fool who's going to get an arrow/spear to the face, but I will assume that wasn't the point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In the context of running a battle, 100 farmers with bronze swords, bronze-tipped spears, and shields, probably practice with their weapons somewhat regularly, have some experience, and some training: We'll call it a Size 3 group of Battle-Ready Troops.<br /> <br /> If that's it (no enemy Exalted commanders, etc), then as a mechanical assessment, in my experience, a group of 4-6 PCs, unless they are unusually bad at combat, absolutely will thrash that Battle Group, though the less well-defended PCs might get crashed.<br /> <br /> With 100 <i>elite</i> troops in medium armour with good weapons, my experience is that the PCs will still win but, especially if there's a commander, the less well-defended PCs might get crashed or even damaged. Depends how many PCs, who they are, how well they're fighting together (I'm talking about groups of PCs, I've seen single Essence 4 PCs be chased off by Battle Groups of elite mortal troops with bows).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I agree with Lioness about the battle groups. If you want the kind of battle where PCs chop through hordes of men, just stick both sides' mortal soldiers into one massive battle group each.*<br /> <br /> *There is the issue that battle groups only go up to, what, 1000? 2000? I forget the exact number. So if you've got 10,000 a side anyway, you may want to do things differently, either more battle groups or have a lot of it off-screen/by ST fiat.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you want to have a bit more complex thing than &quot;PC stabs battle group, battle group stabs PC&quot; x10, then you might want different battle groups for different narrative/kinds of unit. Maybe one for the central infantry, one for the left flank, one for the right flank, and one for the cavalry reserve. Then you can have things like &quot;The left flank is collapsing, send in the reserve!&quot; or &quot;circle round the side and hit their right flank!&quot; Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T03:53:13-07:00","id":1390525,"title":"","content":"{placeholder}","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-21-2020, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T07:27:10-07:00","id":1390548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390525#post1390525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">{placeholder}</div> </div> </div> </div>What typing a post is too passe for you now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway when I ran Ex3 I would typically break down the army by sections. You'd have the Infantry, you'd have the Elites, you'd have Archers, you'd have Cavalry.<br /> <br /> That could give you a Legion/Brigade sized force. And I'd say if you have two Divisions fighting each other with the PCs as part of it, then you only need to stat up the Brigade/Battalion level parts where the PCs are. <br /> <br /> During my campaign, the PC General controlled five Legions. Another PC accompanied one of those, which happened to be fighting at a certain point in the Battle. That Legion, and it's commander, and it's particular foes, got dice rolled in the battle system etc. The other four Legions were &quot;off-screen&quot; as it were, I rolled opposed command checks, and used them with adjustments for force multipliers etc to tell me who was winning.<br /> <br /> TLDR you only really need to worry about the section of the battle that a PC is directly involved in and in almost all situations that'll never be more than a few thousand men vs a few thousand men. I'd then break that down by unit type down to a maximum of 4-5 units, with a lot of them getting a cursory &quot;I'm going to assume this unit commander always gets X successes and I don't need much more than that&quot; just to speed bits up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","user":"Solar","date":". 05-21-2020, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T07:27:51-07:00","id":1390549,"title":"","content":"Troops of different types should probably be in different battle groups, especially if it's relevant to the battle strategy. Like, if the general has 200 hundred archers whose job is to attack from range when the enemy advances, 1000 conscripts who are only really there to die or prevent the enemy from getting within melee range of the archers, and 100 elite troops who are expected to actually win the battle, it's better to have three battle groups because they have very distinct equipment, training, and rolls during the battle.<br /> <br /> If you just want an army for the PCs to fight, you can treat it as one battle group and <i>say</i> there are elite officers commanding the conscripts or archers shooting arrows from the back of the army without giving them separate mechanical effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T07:30:29-07:00","id":1390550,"title":"","content":"I'd also assume that most combat capable PCs are able to take on and beat a S3 Battle Group of decent troops with a solidly competent commander. That's my experience too. So if you want a decent fight add in a champion or two, or add another battlegroup of archers or whatever to make things interesting (although PC vs Battlegroup is not typically very interesting as Battlegroups don't get many combat options)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T08:58:05-07:00","id":1390557,"title":"","content":"I think all the above is good advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T09:06:59-07:00","id":1390559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390548#post1390548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What typing a post is too passe for you now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They took away our delete option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T10:19:51-07:00","id":1390571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390401#post1390401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not quite how DW shakes out all the time. <br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> That seems like it might skip over a bit too much action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, that should be a single, connected thought. My bad on spacing. Link these two statements together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aren't you supposed to discriminate when you have disparate statistics and capabilities? </div> </div> </div>AND distance is <i>supposed</i> to be a factor.<br /> <br /> But unless you are really focusing on the war and running according to Lioness's advice (which is good advice)... you don't gain anything by running four battle groups whose only difference is plus or minus a die or two. It is often bookkeeping for the sake of bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390441#post1390441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In past editions, soldiers that split duties between drill and farming were passingly mentioned as being the solid rank and file that still fell as regular extras, so that might inform a mechanical expectation in this case. I know it informed my response.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha covered fam:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 3E Core Page 496</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Few city-states can afford to maintain standing armies indefinitely, so common troops spend much of the year in agricultural labor, going to war only between harvests or when princes can afford wartime pay.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anyone wants to debate the delination between &quot;farm labourer&quot; and &quot;farmer&quot; or explore the historical prevelance and significance of bronze swords then I am happy to discuss further in a different thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-21-2020, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T10:33:01-07:00","id":1390576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390571#post1390571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But unless you are really focusing on the war and running according to Lioness's advice (which is good advice)... you don't gain anything by running four battle groups who's only difference is plus or minus a die or two. It is often bookkeeping for the sake of bookkeeping.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue that 2 battle size 4 battle groups is probably better than one size 5, and so if you always differentiate you may have players going &quot;I'm going to give half my guys 2-handed spears, and the others shields and axes&quot; just so they can split them into two battle groups. Or have them complain when they summon 10 slightly different first circle demons and you, the ST, insist on making those a Size 1, Might 2, Average Drill Battlegroup, instead of letting them roll 10 different first circle demons into a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T13:46:07-07:00","id":1390616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390576#post1390576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue that 2 battle size 4 battle groups is probably better than one size 5, and so if you always differentiate you may have players going &amp;quot;I'm going to give half my guys 2-handed spears, and the others shields and axes&amp;quot; just so they can split them into two battle groups. Or have them complain when they summon 10 slightly different first circle demons and you, the ST, insist on making those a Size 1, Might 2, Average Drill Battlegroup, instead of letting them roll 10 different first circle demons into a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh it's so much worse than that.<br /> <br /> RAW they can all have 2-handed spears, but when you split them into two flanking groups with some distance between them you can start arguing for two battlegroups. When the system handles this so much neater with a Stratagem and/or Stunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T14:46:32-07:00","id":1390629,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, yeah that's a decent stunt, or indeed yes, using the Pincer Strategem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T18:35:30-07:00","id":1390676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390571#post1390571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, that should be a single, connected thought. My bad on spacing. Link these two statements together.<br /> <br /> <br /> AND distance is <i>supposed</i> to be a factor.<br /> <br /> But unless you are really focusing on the war and running according to Lioness's advice (which is good advice)... you don't gain anything by running four battle groups whose only difference is plus or minus a die or two. It is often bookkeeping for the sake of bookkeeping.</div> </div> </div> </div>My complaint was specifically about very disparate weapons, per the reference to BT infantry rules. I would break an extreme long-range attacker into a different unit from the close combat skirmishers, is what I'm saying. Doctrinally, the archers and slingers are going to be a way smaller group than the bulk of an Imperial or Lookshy legion, like a Size 2 auxiliary that accompanies the main Size 5 unit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gotcha covered fam: </div> </div> </div>I keep forgetting that vague things GCG posted on the internet keep getting explicitly elucidated in parts of later editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T23:51:15-07:00","id":1390717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390318-i-need-advice-on-how-to-run-a-battle-in-exalted?p=1390676#post1390676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My complaint was specifically about very disparate weapons, per the reference to BT infantry rules. I would break an extreme long-range attacker into a different unit from the close combat skirmishers, is what I'm saying. Doctrinally, the archers and slingers are going to be a way smaller group than the bulk of an Imperial or Lookshy legion, like a Size 2 auxiliary that accompanies the main Size 5 unit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally wouldn't.<br /> <br /> If a Realm force of 250 Heavy Infantry, 500 Light Infantry and 250 archers fights an Ice Walker force of 800 Light Infantry and 200 mounted slingers then I'd run each side as a single battle group.<br /> <br /> That number of troops is likely spread out over multiple range bands anyway, and their long range vs close combat capabilities are (more-or-less) balanced against each other. I <i>might</i> just knock two dice from their ranged attacks <i>maybe</i> (only if it became relevant because of PC actions).<br /> <br /> Likewise if it's 30 archers and two spearfighters vs 40 swordfighter then I don't think the two speaefighters are meaningfully contributing enough to the fight to justify a second battlegroup. Just stunt it.<br /> <br /> Looping right back to the OP though... if your army is 100 pressganged peasants with sicles and scythes and 12 elite super soliders geared out with micro howitzers, powered armor and airstriking drones vs a horde of 2000 horse archers... then it MIGHT be worth breaking your forces into two battlegroups.<br /> <br /> I probably still wouldn't. The 100 conscripts can be run as a diceless background element for you to Stunt with. Unless there's a PC with really good War Charms who is able to stack magical bonuses on the conscripts until they are just as deadly as the super soliders... but then if the two units are just as good as each other, I'd be sorely tempted to just run them as a single, larger battlegroup.<br /> <br /> Unless you are personally friends with the archers, and every one who falls in battle will be a meaningful, scaring loss, whereas your spearfighters are disposable human shields, the verisimilitude gained by breaking up close and long range attacks simply isn't worth it. In my opinion, your milage may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}